    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d256-a5">

                <pb facs="0450" n="416" sameAs="frus:frus1870/pg416"/>

                <head>Mr. Holland to the
                        undersecretary of state for foreign affairs.</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Colonial Office,</hi></placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1870-05-13"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >May</hi> 13, 1870.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir:</hi> I am directed by Earl Granville to
                    acknowledge the receipt of your letter of the 9th instant, requesting to be
                    furnished, for communication to the Government of the United States, with copies
                    of the instructions issued to the commanders of the Canadian vessels engaged in
                    the protection of the fisheries.</p>
                <p>Lord Granville desires me to state, for the information of Lord Clarendon, that
                    the Governor General of the Dominion has been requested by telegraph to forward
                    to this office any instructions already issued on this subject, or that may be
                    issued in consequence of Lord Granville’s dispatch to the Governor General, of
                    which a copy is inclosed.</p>
                <p>I am, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>H. HOLLAND,</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
